{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_24\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 24</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Solution_2_simplified)_-_Come_and_Go_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Solution 2 simplified) - Come and Go Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_-_Thought_Process\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 - Thought Process</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_24\">Problem 24</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 24\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The notation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> (read \"n factorial\") is defined as the product of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive integers. (For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/a/94a242fd4e0b4340266b9452ed2b56ffbf4d32c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!=1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" />). Define the superfactorial of a positive integer, denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/a/02a97a9c283fc8c4bd1694c81762d741d5724175.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, to be the product of the factorials of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> integers. (For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc8189963a9a069c188ac5bdc8cbde64ca19dab4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^!=1! \\cdot 2! \\cdot 3! = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"151\" height=\"17\" />). How many factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> appear in the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/8/1e89688c53c0c11bfa5caa6eda36798731828da6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51^!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" />, the superfactorial of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1fd7cb028e27b8648efbfb002f3e6d4fcb33a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f61dc9bbd2b8bf88d5275be93185e017f789ef7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 147 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 150 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 156 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 168 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 171$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Solution_2_simplified.29_-_Come_and_Go_Solution\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Solution_2_simplified)_-_Come_and_Go_Solution\">Solution 1 (Solution 2 simplified) - Come and Go Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Solution 2 simplified) - Come and Go Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55b0a0d17a33640a4e1692569d45b5ff8479f60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7! - 13!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />, there is one power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/d/7adab344e7ba5d39a83e391cdce57086659c35d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14! - 20!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/7/fa7ad829c641de786ff595494a5015e29b4414cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21! - 27!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/0/e306ddba9583fbee7f7d7d1cc12b3c0615d61c44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28! - 34!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/4/f44f15065be204d5bb48ad015c123824c7f9c53a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35! - 41!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea147a44af272012b623a31c8804753d2674b130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42! - 48!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers. Finally, from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e369e0018648e3a99fade3321c6f9bfbb82049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02fc4a2e9473bb0b24d416c78d433d4c791bd0b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers (as each one contributes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/026bb71c09708994ead7a4ee100a03960a87c4f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />). Thus, in a superfactorial, the number of powers is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192dffb66b8a61fbf0bf04d350d5048974954c3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7+14+21+28+35+42+24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"253\" height=\"15\" /> powers total, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf22ad3a1ab8f94088893c936b2c0ec66f39d816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{171}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p>In another way, we can think of it like 7 multiples. For example, from seven to thirteen there happens to exist 7 7's. Later from 14 to 20 there happens to exist 7*2 sevens. When we continue to move on to 49 and 51, there exists an extra seven because of the squares. Adding them up we should get 171 as our answer.\n</p><p>Note for Jellycat88: That logic is flawed. Definition of multiples always implies one factor of seven. your idea works as long as the value is not a perfect square. for instance, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad9b353876051665380a678796ede088a587bfa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c1408c98668f8913671ca718ac80fab5ae886a70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />, each corresponds two multiples of seven, those being 7 and 14. when you count that extra square, you are counting a power not a multiple, because from 49 to 51, we obtain only seven multiples, 7,14,21,28,35,42,49. However, from 49 through 51, we obtain eight <b>powers</b>. it is a minor yet huge difference, which is why your logic is slightly flawed.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_-_Thought_Process\">Solution 2 - Thought Process</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 - Thought Process\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We begin by noticing that for the first few factorials (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21c931311c845f583d325ba3e863252cfe388b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/6/e26ca46a67d19ce2e5b692103305a083a2361fd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />) there are no factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, because the first multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> itself. So, these numbers contribute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sevens.\n</p><p>The next <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factorials (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/1/ce11f9bca5e74ba532323e045b62e2793d120b7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651c6746e6615c978821ad9350dab20e297166d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />) all have one factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in them, since every number less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is multiplied in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. These all contribute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sevens.\n</p><p>For the next <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factorials (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad9b353876051665380a678796ede088a587bfa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfe8ffbaf55875f55dd581143da6b8bb90c376b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20!$\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />), there are two factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />). These numbers contribute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> sevens.\n</p><p>If we continue with this method, we see that once we hit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/2/4924a689c01edc24514b80ccc6d07f480505b325.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7k!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/2/1c2d97b164f6f0adb33315e88175f831b441888c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> sevens contributed, since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers in between. This will work from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21c931311c845f583d325ba3e863252cfe388b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/6/3d689eb0afafebf7cadad9d9c2727748c3b2615a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, because when we get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d0f513fb6a7112b99fbeca0f194d6d410aca84c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49! = (7^2)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"21\" />, we have one extra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for every number, since we have an extra factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>This is only for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e369e0018648e3a99fade3321c6f9bfbb82049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/8/d48ed7b060a90510dbdd4ac1daf83459b88dccad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50!$\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02fc4a2e9473bb0b24d416c78d433d4c791bd0b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> (our final factorial). They have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/3/f331a7262c097e1130830f0416c58f880a2d9db4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7+1 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, because they have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and one extra from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c8e6bf4d57cd6f2bb0d7d43e00f0f442f53b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />. These three contribute a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/4/5343ceef50cf28d4bfbf391e509688af25beb3d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 8 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> sevens.\n</p><p>Finally, sum these numbers. Most are just the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and we can calculate this sum to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/e/c6eb79c2320bec376aa1918847879e9eee94e410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 + 7 + 14 + 21 + \\dots + 42 = 7 \\cdot \\frac{6(6+1)}{2} = 7 \\cdot \\frac{42}{2} = 7 \\cdot 21 = 147$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"506\" height=\"40\" />. The final step is to add the final <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/7/d674b359bd10b1837146dd0f18515c1d264389ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot 8 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> sevens to get our answer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/681f9c0bb40c17e15248b8b22261569b65fe6c1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$147 + 24 = \\boxed{ \\textbf{(E) } 171}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"166\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~OlympiadMaster\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d9299234be7fda0e00a85e8ae335e6189600ac25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51^! = 1! \\cdot 2! \\cdot ... \\cdot 51! = (1) (1 \\cdot 2)(1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3)(...)(1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot ... \\cdot 51)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"472\" height=\"22\" /> is expanded as such, each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/205462547824cd31d00ed88aebeed00057972d4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\leq 51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> will appear once in each of the expansions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/6/f16a8ae1bda8e5566a60048a628687b29e21649d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{k!, ..., 51!\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/6/2862bbd3bb865d409ee5b1551e411aba62848538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> appearances.  \n</p><p>Therefore, in this expansion, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> appears <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> appears <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5e2e4c4950cff11894abd202aa2949e21819c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> times, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> appears <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> appears <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> appears <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> appears <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c8e6bf4d57cd6f2bb0d7d43e00f0f442f53b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> appears <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times.  Except for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c8e6bf4d57cd6f2bb0d7d43e00f0f442f53b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, which contributes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> copies of the factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, each of these terms contributes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> copy of the factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/7/aa74d9ebd69cac7665e69bd40fa1c24fe19b282a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45 + 38 + 31 + 24 + 17 + 10 + 3 \\cdot 2 = \\boxed{ \\textbf{(E) } 171}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" /> copies of the factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can count how many multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> appear throughout the expression. The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> appears from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/1/ce11f9bca5e74ba532323e045b62e2793d120b7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02fc4a2e9473bb0b24d416c78d433d4c791bd0b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5e8dc508c48acc4e1ccd60e85a6628ae8c4d0ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51 - 7 + 1 = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" /> times. The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> appears from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad9b353876051665380a678796ede088a587bfa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02fc4a2e9473bb0b24d416c78d433d4c791bd0b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/4704182c80daba3afb48a7488a436268d3a97db3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51 - 14 + 1 = 38$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" /> times. \n</p><p>If we continue this, we find that the total is the sum of numbers decreasing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> each time: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91a8d27d49604ce9c35552f88401b778016e7159.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[45 + 38 + 31 + 24 + 17 + 10 + 3 = 168\\]\" width=\"301\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de9b314d77b0fa0b0caeac11a9934fab71c1ce12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49 = 7^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />, we count an extra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e369e0018648e3a99fade3321c6f9bfbb82049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/8/d48ed7b060a90510dbdd4ac1daf83459b88dccad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50!$\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02fc4a2e9473bb0b24d416c78d433d4c791bd0b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />. Adding these three extra factors gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f8202b5e97cd1697cb9f3f3a868b47bc7587c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[168 + 3 = \\mathbf{171}\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/b/a0bb7d4574191caa7e1d30134cf632ba33b35184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E) 171}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"68\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Frigate\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/d5YE9m2D4IY\">https://youtu.be/d5YE9m2D4IY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=3015s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=3015s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?